// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6313 new: Potential Container Escape Via Docker Socket Or Host Namespace Access
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6313
// Pull request author: aaronsawit
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Container Escape Via Docker Socket Or Host Namespace Access
// Sigma ID: 0efe4005-85b1-46f0-a83c-3c942cfe455a
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Aaron Sawit
// Date: 2026-09-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, execution, T1611, T1610
// Description: Detects the start of a container that shares the host PID namespace, mounts the Docker socket or
//   the host root filesystem, or is granted the SYS_ADMIN capability. Each of these options removes
//   a part of the isolation between the container and the host and is a well-known path to escape
//   from a container to the host. An attacker with access to the Docker CLI or API can use these
//   options to gain root privileges on the host. Some monitoring agents, reverse proxies and
//   container management tools legitimately require these options. It is recommended to baseline
//   those and filter them by image name.
// False positives:
//   - Monitoring agents, reverse proxies and container management tools that require access to the Docker socket
//   - Administrators debugging the host from a container
// References:
//   - https://docs.docker.com/engine/security/
//   - https://docs.docker.com/engine/containers/run/
//   - https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Docker_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html
//   - https://blog.trailofbits.com/2019/07/19/understanding-docker-container-escapes/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/7c55f069b9ee54ff104a49fee719ea7ebbf89ea2/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_container_host_access_flags.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/docker" or FolderPath endswith "/nerdctl" or FolderPath endswith "/podman") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " create " or ProcessCommandLine contains " run ") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "--cap-add SYS_ADMIN" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--cap-add=SYS_ADMIN" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--pid host" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--pid=host" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-v /:/" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--volume /:/" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/var/run/docker.sock:" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/run/docker.sock:")
